<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria offers 3.0 bln levs 42-day T-bills Oct 11.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria offers 3.0 bln levs 42-day T-bills Oct 11.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer three billion levs of 42-day floater coupon T-bills at an auction on Friday, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry, a BNB statement said.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at an annual 300 percent.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	 BG 3019196024</p>
<p> Type		   Floater coupon</p>
<p> Par value	    3.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	 October 11, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	   October 17, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	November 28, 1996</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
